        </gmd:CI_Citation>
      </gmd:citation>
      <gmd:abstract>
        <gco:CharacterString>Fire Weather Index (FWI) from ECMWF reanalysis data. The FWI is a numerical rating of fire intensity and potential fire behavior, based on weather conditions such as temperature, humidity, wind speed, and precipitation. It is commonly used in wildfire management and forecasting to assess fire risk and guide firefighting efforts.</gco:CharacterString>
      </gmd:abstract>
